`l` is not used after this call, so a compiled program closes the listener here, before the next line runs: a connection to its port is refused. (The interpreter keeps it open, so the program behaves differently there.) Use `l` again where you are done with it, for example `Socket.close_listener(l)`. [listener_closed_early]

